# Rules moved — do not keep rules in this file

This project's rules now live in the files the agents actually load:

- `AGENTS.md` (root) — the law: ask when unsure, evidence never assertion, spend
  tokens sparingly, report short and in Arabic. Commands included.
- `.clinerules/graphify.md` — query the local code graph before reading many files.
- `.clinerules/workflow.md` — the routine around an edit, and the reporting shape.
- `.clinerules/testing.md` — what the tests cover, and when a test is the wrong answer.
- `.clinerules/style.md` — comments, the shared palette, layout constants, RTL traps.
- `.clinerules/docs.md` — when the memory files get updated.
- `docs/AGENTS.md` — the deep handbook: build, boot, services, Firestore, gotchas.

This stub exists only so an editor that reads `.cursorrules` lands somewhere
useful. It is intentionally empty of rules: rules in two places drift, and that is
exactly how this project's navbar height and sidebar height ended up disagreeing.
Put new rules in the files above instead.
